{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed all deliverables.\n\nThe evidence rejects a baseline-artifact interpretation for binary crime: changing the reference only reverses the ±25.1-point AMCE. Baseline-invariant MMs are 62.6% versus 37.4%. Crime has the largest observed spread, but only narrowly exceeds driving time’s 23.7 points, so the memo claims a large effect—not unique dominance.\n\n- [script.R](/Users/scdenney/Documents/github/resources/ai-for-research/demos/orchestration-lab/runs/46-sol-v2/t3/script.R)\n- [sensitivity.png](/Users/scdenney/Documents/github/resources/ai-for-research/demos/orchestration-lab/runs/46-sol-v2/t3/figures/sensitivity.png)\n- [sensitivity-table.md](/Users/scdenney/Documents/github/resources/ai-for-research/demos/orchestration-lab/runs/46-sol-v2/t3/sensitivity-table.md)\n- [memo.md](/Users/scdenney/Documents/github/resources/ai-for-research/demos/orchestration-lab/runs/46-sol-v2/t3/memo.md)\n- [routing-log.md](/Users/scdenney/Documents/github/resources/ai-for-research/demos/orchestration-lab/runs/46-sol-v2/t3/routing-log.md)\n\nFinal verification passed: `Rscript script.R` succeeds, the sole figure is 320 dpi with no title, and the memo is approximately 400 words. The routing log records all three delegation calls, including the Claude `fable` check and Terra sandbox handling."}}
